From: Amazing A32 kernel bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: do not make GCC string truncation diagnostics fatal

This vendor tree deliberately builds kernel/ with -Werror. Newer GCC versions
diagnose several long-standing strncpy patterns as -Wstringop-truncation,
including kernel/power/qos.c and kernel/printk/printk.c. These diagnostics were
not emitted by the toolchains this 4.9 tree originally targeted.

Keep -Werror for the rest of kernel/, but leave this newer warning class as a
warning when the compiler supports the option.

--- a/kernel/Makefile
+++ b/kernel/Makefile
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 # Makefile for the linux kernel.
 #
 
 subdir-ccflags-y += -Werror
+subdir-ccflags-y += $(call cc-option,-Wno-error=stringop-truncation)
 subdir-ccflags-y += -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/include
 subdir-ccflags-y += -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/include/mt-plat
 subdir-ccflags-y += -I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/mtprof
